color of an element."}],"title":"color","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLColor","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLOtherDirection":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLOtherDirection"}],"title":"MXLOtherDirection","abstract":[{"text":"The other-direction type is used to define any direction symbols not yet in the MusicXML format. The smufl","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute can be used to specify a particular direction symbol, allowing application interoperability without","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"requiring every SMuFL glyph to have a MusicXML element equivalent. Using the other-direction type without the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"smufl attribute allows for extended representation, though without application interoperability.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOtherDirection","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlotherdirection","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLOtherDirection"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"}}}